pinyon-shift-fh1-render-test-v1
# Output-frame paced, synchronized on game state, from a seed without a
# profile (fresh-2026-09-28, run with --fresh-profile): the new-player
# opening. Wait for the title asset (including a recent open), then press Start
# and enter the single-player menu. Longer bounded waits cover splash/movie
# wall time even when the renderer outputs frames much faster than 60 Hz. Then,
# once the opening event's route has loaded (trackroute170.xml), the controls
# screen, the intro and the opening drive in the Viper: the second race event
# of the matrix; the intro cinematic runs on wall time, so the drive captures
# keep a margin after it. A is pressed every 300 frames, as the launcher's shader
# preparation route does, to pass each screen.
